# One-slice weight prefetch for the two owning projection kernels.
#
# A block's two weight words are loaded in the slice that uses them, so they issue behind that
# slice's fragment loads and the operand expansion waits on the whole outstanding queue.
# Fetching them one slice ahead lets the expansion wait on two words instead.
#
# Measured in research/ffn/batched/tile-ownership: worth 1.87 -> 1.30 ms on the down projection
# at 256 rows in that directory's own kernel. On these two kernels the compiler already schedules
# most of it: across runs at 256 rows, layer 0, arith-iu4-a4 moved 3.285 -> 3.185 ms and
# arith-iu8-a8 4.433 -> 4.365 ms, while cs-scaled-f16-a8 did not move (4.014 -> 4.006 ms) against
# 0.6-1.0% run-to-run drift on unchanged candidates. Output hashes are unchanged.
#
# Apply from the repository root:  git apply research/ffn/batched/tile-ownership/one-slice-prefetch.patch
#
# The two paired-FP16 branches of arith_maps.hip take the same change and are not included.

diff --git a/research/ffn/batched/arithmetic/candidates/arith_maps.hip b/research/ffn/batched/arithmetic/candidates/arith_maps.hip
index 7fc048c..da01319 100644
